; pattern-basic: :pattern as the third track source, queried on the bar
; grid (1 cycle = 1 bar, identity). The case exists for wasm parity —
; hap selection and the seeded rand kernel must be byte-identical native
; vs wasm32. No :dur/:end loop: the clock advances freely so the
; pattern's own cycle math (tick mod PPC) drives the bar wrap; a
; transport loop would pin every frame to cycle 0 and erase the
; alternation / rand-across-cycles signal.
(transport :bpm 120 :meter [4 4])

; fastcat: four quarter-bar slots, the third silent. The silent slot
; OMITS the write (a gap) while the sibling tracks still land, so parity
; must agree on which frames produce a write.
(track :target grid :pattern [0.1 0.2 (silence) 0.4])

; slowcat: one child per cycle — 0.25 on even cycles, 0.75 on odd —
; pinning alternation across the bar wrap.
(track :target alt :pattern (slowcat 0.25 0.75))

; seeded rand: one hap per cycle valued rand01(seed, cycle). The whole
; reason parity matters here — SJON's deterministic rand kernel must
; yield the identical float on wasm32, and distinct floats per cycle.
(track :target noise :pattern (pure (rand01 seed cycle)))

; euclid: E(3,8) = x..x..x. (the tresillo) — 0.8 in onset slots 0/3/6,
; gaps elsewhere. Pins SJON's Bjorklund desugar through pacer's lane:
; the existing times hit an onset (0.00), a rest (0.50 — slot 2), the
; second onset (0.75 — slot 3), and the bar wrap back onto slot 0.
(track :target pulse :pattern (euclid 3 8 0.8))
